SUMMARY:Streamyfin v0.55.2
DESCRIPTION:Streamyfin 0.55.2 | streamyfin-ios\n\n## What's Changed\n\n0.55
 .2 is another bug fix release. One thing does change: a TV is now signed i
 n from your phone with Quick Connect\, so Quick Connect has to be on in yo
 ur server's dashboard (it is by default) and both devices need this versio
 n. The rest again comes out of the crash and error reports\, plus a round 
 of fixes to accounts and the Seerr sign-in\n\nThanks to everyone who repor
 ted a problem\, and to @Gauvino for the Quick Connect and Seerr fixes!\n\n
 ### ✨ Highlights\n- **Signing a TV in from your phone uses Quick Connect
 **\, with a code or a QR code\, and no longer sends your password over the
  local network (#2240) by @Gauvino\n- **Freezes of a few seconds when play
 back starts or resumes** on iOS and tvOS are fixed (#2205) by @fredrikburm
 ester\n- **Access tokens are kept out of the app log**\, including the log
 s you export\, and entries written by earlier versions are cleaned up (#21
 03) by @Gauvino\n- **Seerr access no longer carries over** to the next acc
 ount signed in on the same device (#2233) by @Gauvino\n- **Quick Connect i
 n Settings** sends the code on its sixth digit and tells you why a code fa
 ils (#2246) by @Gauvino\n- **Luxembourgish** is available as an app langua
 ge (#2195) by @Gauvino\n\n### 🎬 Player\n- iOS and tvOS: the app no long
 er freezes for several seconds when playback starts or resumes while the s
 ystem audio service is slow to answer (#2205) by @fredrikburmester\n- Musi
 c: tapping a track far down the queue before the rest has loaded no longer
  fails\, and neither do previous and next with repeat all (#2212) by @fred
 rikburmester\n\n### 📺 TV\n- Pairing a TV with a phone goes through Quic
 k Connect: the TV shows a code and a QR code\, your phone approves it\, an
 d the TV signs in by itself. No password travels between the two devices\,
  and the TV picks its own server (#2240) by @Gauvino\n- On the phone\, Set
 tings > Log in on TV scans the QR code or takes the code typed in\, and th
 e entry now shows on iPhones too (#2240) by @Gauvino\n- T
URL:https://raynmahbub.github.io/OmniSource/feeds/streamyfin.json
